Okay then, let's set up Secure Boot. Thankfully, you can use this script and do not
have to go through this ordeal on your own.

We are setting up Secure Boot before enrolling additional secrets for LUKS,
because using the TPM as a secret in many cases requires binding to the Secure
Boot state (don't worry if you do not know what any of that means).

Before, we start let's install a couple of packages that we will need in the
process.